Troye Sivan’s ‘She’s the Best’ Album: All 12 Tracks&nbsp;Ranked

Troye Sivan Talks &#8216;Chaotic&#8217; New Album & Getting Madonna&#8217;s Approval for &#8216;Party&#8217;: &#8216;I Was Pleasantly Surprised&#8217;

In his Friday (Oct. 9) interview with Billboard , the Aussie singer opened up about why he wanted the Oscar winner to star in his &#8220;She&#8217;s the Best&#8221; music video while shouting out ADÉLA&#8217;s hit &#8220;Nicole Kidman,&#8221; which recently reached a new peak at No. 11 on the Billboard Hot 100 . &#8220;I was just listening to, &#8216;Every single night…,'&#8221; Sivan began, singing some of the Slovak star&#8217;s lyrics.

&#8220;Nicole is &#8212; I haven&#8217;t spoken to ADÉLA about the song &#8212; but I think maybe for the same reason she wrote that song,&#8221; he continued. &#8220;Nicole represents something, I think, to so many people that is kind of unexplainable. There&#8217;s an energy there that&#8217;s so captivating. She&#8217;s such a good example of the women I&#8217;ve been obsessed with my entire life.&#8221;

ADÉLA recently shared similar thoughts with Billboard and acknowledged how &#8220;wild&#8221; it is that Kidman &#8212; who&#8217;s voiced support for the song named after her &#8212; is in her corner. In his conversation with Billboard , Sivan similarly expressed how present and engaged the actress was throughout the production of the &#8220;She&#8217;s the Best&#8221; visual &#8212; even though he was convinced that Kidman wouldn&#8217;t be able to show up on the day of, given how in-demand she is.

&#8220;I was like, &#8216;I&#8217;m going to believe it when we wrap the video,'&#8221; he recalled. &#8220;It&#8217;s Nicole Kidman! Something&#8217;s going to come up. Every time my phone would go off, and it was her name, I was like, &#8216;F&#8211;k, here it is.'&#8221;

The chat arrives on the same day as Sivan&#8217;s new album, She&#8217;s the Best , which comes three years after his Billboard 200 No. 20 full-length Something to Give Each Other . One of the project&#8217;s cornerstones, he said, is celebrating the women &#8212; such as Kidman &#8212; whom he&#8217;s spent his life admiring.

Sivan added that he made one of the songs, &#8220;Canada Dry,&#8221; to capture &#8220;this specific feeling of pop music that I love, which is, like, slinky sexy.&#8221;

&#8220;I feel like Addison (Rae) does a really great job of it,&#8221; he noted. &#8220;Janet (Jackson) is sort of the queen at it, Kylie (Minogue) is amazing at it.&#8221;

Madonna gets her flowers on the LP as Sivan samples her Billboard Hot 100 topper &#8220;Music&#8221; in his single &#8220;Party.&#8221; He shouted out the Queen of Pop for making it so &#8220;easy&#8221; to clear the rights to the track. Good thing, too, considering how badly he wanted to include it.

&#8220;Before you hear the &#8216;Music&#8217; sample, there&#8217;s this almost vacuum where the track cuts out and cuts to me breathing, as if I&#8217;m heaving on a dance floor,&#8221; he explained to Billboard . &#8220;Then &#8216;Music&#8217; by Madonna creeps in, and in my head, it&#8217;s like I&#8217;m on the dance floor closing my eyes, having one of those moments where I feel like I&#8217;m ascending. I had this story in my head, and then I got so attached to it, and I was so nervous. But Madonna somehow made it very easy and said yes pretty much right away.&#8221;

Sivan also addressed whether he cares about releasing songs that spark polarizing opinions, specifically such as &#8220;She&#8217;s the Best.&#8221; &#8220;No, it&#8217;s kind of what I want,&#8221; he said. &#8220;I&#8217;ve never really strived for a &#8216;hit&#8217; in my career &#8212; I&#8217;ve never really had one, to be honest. I feel like a song like &#8216;Rush&#8217; changed my life so much more than a song like &#8216;Youth&#8217; did.

&#8220;Coming off the back of a project that was as pop as my last one, I kind of wanted a reclamation of, &#8216;I still don&#8217;t have interest in playing the pop game, really.&#8217; I liked the idea of doing something that was for me.&#8221;

